{
  "feature": "expressions",
  "name": "Confusion (natural)",
  "part": {
    "schema": "xfs/expression-part-1",
    "body": {
      "label": "Confused",
      "controls": {
        "eye_l_brows_lateral": 0.5,
        "eye_l_brows_lower": 0.55,
        "eye_l_oculi_squint_inner": 0.4,
        "eye_r_brows_lateral": 0.3,
        "eye_r_brows_lower": 0.1,
        "eye_r_brows_raise_in": 0.3,
        "eye_r_brows_raise_out": 0.55,
        "eye_r_oculi_squint_inner": 0.15,
        "eye_r_widen": 0.1,
        "lips_chin_raise": 0.25,
        "lips_mid_shift_r": 0.3,
        "lips_r_corner_dn": 0.1,
        "lips_r_corner_wide": 0.3
      },
      "links": {
        "eye_brows_lateral": false,
        "eye_brows_lower": false,
        "eye_brows_raise_in": false,
        "eye_brows_raise_out": false,
        "eye_oculi_squint_inner": false,
        "eye_widen": false,
        "lips_corner_dn": false,
        "lips_corner_wide": false
      },
      "origin": {
        "kind": "rest"
      }
    }
  },
  "facs": {
    "closestVanilla": "facial_pissed",
    "actionUnits": [
      {
        "au": "AU4",
        "name": "Brow lowerer",
        "intensity": "C (left) / A (right)",
        "note": "Corrugator and depressor: the brows knit, one side much more.",
        "controls": [
          "eye_l_brows_lower",
          "eye_r_brows_lower",
          "eye_l_brows_lateral",
          "eye_r_brows_lateral"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU1+2",
        "name": "Inner and outer brow raiser (right only)",
        "intensity": "C",
        "note": "The other brow goes up: the questioning brow.",
        "controls": [
          "eye_r_brows_raise_out",
          "eye_r_brows_raise_in"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU7",
        "name": "Lid tightener",
        "intensity": "B (left)",
        "controls": [
          "eye_l_oculi_squint_inner",
          "eye_r_oculi_squint_inner"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU5",
        "name": "Upper lid raiser (right)",
        "intensity": "A",
        "controls": [
          "eye_r_widen"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU14",
        "name": "Dimpler (unilateral)",
        "intensity": "B",
        "note": "The mouth pulls to one side.",
        "controls": [
          "lips_r_corner_wide",
          "lips_mid_shift_r"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU15",
        "name": "Lip corner depressor (right)",
        "intensity": "A",
        "controls": [
          "lips_r_corner_dn"
        ]
      },
      {
        "au": "AU17",
        "name": "Chin raiser",
        "intensity": "B",
        "controls": [
          "lips_chin_raise"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "why": [
      "Confusion is carried by the brows: AU4 knits and lowers them, and it is the most reported action unit for confusion in the literature.",
      "One brow down and the other up makes the face a question rather than anger. Vanilla faces with knitted brows (furious, pissed) lower both brows hard.",
      "The mouth stays closed and is pulled to one side (unilateral AU14) with a small chin raise (AU17): puzzled, not upset."
    ],
    "source": "XF Studio experiment 026 (research/animation/natural-expressions.md): authored values, tuned in the live preview."
  }
}
